==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|rock-paper-scissors}}

===Etymology===
After the handshapes, as a {{calque|en|ja|じゃんけんぽん|tr=jankenpon|nocap=1}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|games}} A popular children's [[game]] using three [[hand]] [[sign]]s representing rock, paper and scissors, frequently used as a [[tiebreaker]].
#: {{syn|en|paper scissors stone|scissors paper rock|scissors paper stone|janken|roshambo}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Any situation where [[strategy|strategies]] are not [[transitive]], meaning each strategy is strong against some strategies and weak against others in a loop such that there is no universally best option.

